      "id": "claim_d2bb1ed4e86c4f10924302843dc64de2",
      "statement": "Pressure shedding is a pure classifier over a memory sample plus the prior shedding state; each ceiling (`CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB` and the 95%-of-machine cgroup charge cap) latches and releases at its own watermark, and the core holds the latch so a sample sequence is replayable.",
